  <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://documentcloud.adobe.com/spodintegration/index.html?locale=en-us">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CDKN technical report year 2 2024 ( 6 July 2023 to 5 July 2024)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Now in year 2, the Climate and Development Knowledge Network (CDKN) can report significant progress in its third phase: Accelerating inclusive climate action. To date, it has produced 37 knowledge products, engaged 3,757 key actors and climate knowledge brokers (approx 56% women) in its knowledge sharing and capacity strengthening activities, secured 40 new partnerships and kicked off 11 Knowledge-to-Action (K2A) projects supporting locally-led adaptation (LLA) in eight countries in Africa and Latin America. 515 organisations have been involved in CDKN&#x2019;s capacity strengthening work. CDKN has already overshot the mid-term target for capacity strengthening, knowledge sharing and partnership activities.  CDKN is now supporting adaptation and resilience building in nine African countries that span both Anglophone and Francophone regions: Benin, Cameroon, Ethiopia, Ghana, Kenya, Mozambique, Namibia, Senegal and South Sudan. Across Africa, Asia, Latin America and at global levels, the respective teams have established or further strengthened relationships with target key actors, including with a range of local and grassroots organisations in Africa and Latin America in supporting LLA, a number of municipalities in South Asia, water funds in Latin America, national governments in Namibia and Ethiopia, county governments in Kenya, young climate leaders and youth groups in Ghana and Ethiopia, and multiple UN agencies and knowledge networks at international levels. In the reporting period, CDKN also contracted ENDA Energie in Senegal to lead CDKN&#x2019;s work in that country, CDKN&#x2019;s first partnership within the Francophone region.</narrative>
   </description>
